We need to answer user: "Explain in three short paragraphs why the sky is blue and why sunsets are red." Need final with three short paragraphs. Ensure exactly three paragraphs? Yes. Short. Explain Rayleigh scattering, blue sky, red sunsets due to longer path, scattering removes blue/green, red/orange remains. Maybe mention Mie? Keep concise.
</think>

The sky is blue because sunlight scatters off molecules in the atmosphere. Shorter blue wavelengths scatter much more strongly than longer red wavelengths, so blue light is spread across the sky and reaches our eyes from all directions.

At sunset, sunlight travels through a much thicker layer of air to reach us. This longer path scatters away most of the blue and green light before it reaches our eyes.

What remains is the longer-wavelength red and orange light, which is why sunsets and sunrises often appear red, orange, or pink.<|im_end|>
